  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWe will enjoy a stretch of quiet weather through Saturday as\nbroad and weak trough remains in place aloft with high \npressure building at the sfc supporting very comfortable \ntemperatures and low humidity. Low temperatures tonight and \ntomorrow night will be great opportunities to open the windows \nas ideal radiational cooling will support overnight \ntemperatures falling into the 40s and 50s. Patchy fog will also\nlikely develop in typically valley areas both night. \n\nTemperatures trend slightly above normal this weekend with\nhumidity levels also creeping upwards early next week as high \npressure slides off shore and southwest flow advects a milder \nair mass northeastward. However, the probability for temperatures\nto exceed 90 degrees remains very low (under 20%) Sunday through\nTuesday across eastern NY and western New England with HeatRisk\nalso only in the \"Minor\" category. Weak troughing returns \nSunday into early next week supporting slight chance and chance \nPOPs for showers and thunderstorms each day through Wednesday. \nThere are signs for a stronger shortwave to swing into the \nNortheast in the Tuesday to Wednesday time period. While there \nis strong consensus among the ensemble guidance for measurable \nprecipitation to occur across eastern NY and western New England\nboth days, the probability for high rainfall amounts (greater \nthan 1 inch in a 24hr period) remains very low.",
